WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.768
Let's go over to Kyiv there.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.736
And, Melissa, security

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.537
assistance is going to be coming

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.372
where it goes.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.706
It's going to make a big difference here

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.974
because it could be compromised

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.376
in at least one key area.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.443
There's a critical bridge

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.745
that last remaining

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:12.512
supply route

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.980
in and out of the city of Bakhmut

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.582
was blown up

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:18.451
That's right.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.519
Incredibly difficult

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.454
now, Bianna, for Ukrainian forces

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.223
to resupply their men

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.824
that are still in the center of town.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.392
They tell us it

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.160
is, though, a matter of time.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.194
What we heard from one soldier

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.229
today is that it could take two

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.397
days, could take 20 days.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.765
The question is how long

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.732
they can hold out

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.767
in the face of these

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.835
ever more experienced foreign mercenaries

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:36.669
and Russian troops

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.871
that have been flooding in

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.972
in a determined effort

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:39.906
to take the home of Obama

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.207
with huge questions.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.842
Be on, of course, about the four

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.677
and a half thousand civilians

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.279
still trapped inside

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:46.880
and there have been

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.515
those pleas over the last few weeks

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.417
on the part of the Ukrainian military

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.318
for more ammunition.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.386
There will be a retreat

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.854
at some point westwards.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:55.622
But what we're seeing

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.656
also right now,

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.224
even as the fate of Obama

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:58.792
that hangs in

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.193
the balance, is further along

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.861
that front line to the south.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.264
These images of a Russian fighter jet

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.733
taken down by Ukrainian

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.902
the Ukrainian military,

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.837
we hear that from the Ukrainian side.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.572
We see it on the images coming in.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.174
We're also hearing those reports

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.842
on Russian state media

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.976
And that is significant,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.144
of course, because what it does

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.945
show us beyond

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.780
is that the Ukrainian air

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.781
defense systems,

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.982
as much as they need

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.384
the patriot systems that are to

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.452
come online shortly

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.820
and that Ukrainian forces

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.854
are being trained on

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:28.922
even now,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.123
have already seen

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.058
an extraordinary improvement in their air

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:32.992
defense systems.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.260
It is several hundred

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.563
Russian plane of fighter planes

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.164
that they say they've taken down now.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.032
And they point out

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.101
that every Russian fighter

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.102
plane on their territory

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.303
is a legitimate target.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.170
That one

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.438
was just flying over

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.339
Donetsk region

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.041
in those occupied territory.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.776
So those weapons

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:50.543
that we've been talking

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.711
about every step of the way

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.613
have come in to try and counter

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.447
exactly the next

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.849
step of the Russian offensive

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.451
when it comes to the air defense systems.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.953
There's a lot more to do,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.955
but this is one of the signs

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:02.822
that it has improved

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.424
and it is working beyond a victor.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.024
You know, Russia's

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.092
offensive has been underway,

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.894
we're told, since early this year.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.295
Melissa Bell and Phil Mattingly,

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.363
thank you both.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:10.830
Joining us now

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.631
to discuss further,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.766
CNN global affairs analyst Kim Doja.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.535
She's also senior managing editor

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.803
at the Military Times.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.705
Also with us, retired Army Brigadier

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.340
General Peter Zack.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.074
Welcome, both of you.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.275
Can, let me start with you

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.176
because Germany

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.111
is arguably the most important player

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.980
here, aside from the United States.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.748
It's Europe's largest economy.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.016
And it had been criticized

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:32.685
early in this war for hesitating

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.388
in providing some of the higher scale

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.422
military assistance.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.491
Obviously, they've increased their aid

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.560
and they are sending those leopard tanks.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.995
But now, as this war enters

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.896
its second year

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.597
and in this conversation, here

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.533
with the president of the United States,

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:46.900
is there

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.301
concern going into it

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.436
that Germany may remain hesitant

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:51.738
in the months ahead?

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:54.507
Well, the answer

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.876
this is a chance for the chancellor

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.510
to explain

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.778
directly to Biden

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.315
why he dragged his feet on coming up with

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.783
those leopard tanks for instance,

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.351
which meant that delayed the U.S.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.853
announcement that it was going to send

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.821
the M1 Abrams tanks.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.090
Germany, like Biden, in a sense,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.359
is facing a situation

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.894
where the German people

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:15.628
are growing

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.731
reluctant to continue supporting this war

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.433
in that their own fears

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.467
seem to be rising.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.803
According to recent polls,

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.005
Fears that the war could spill over

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.440
into the rest of Europe, fears

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.410
that any sort of nuclear confrontation

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.179
could literally blow into their country.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.048
And that kind of thing.

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.950
It means that

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.851
in some senses, Schultz's hands are tied.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.220
He's got to make

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.287
a good argument

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.256
before every single tranche of aid

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.490
he hands out.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.358
Biden is,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.627
in some senses facing the same thing.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.730
And yet Biden must also be asking.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:51.998
The U.S.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.300
has given roughly two times

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.868
as much as all of Europe

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.438
combined in terms of aid to Ukraine.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.340
He's got to be asking Germany.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.442
What else can you ante up?

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:03.543
Hmm.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.045
And what would be most crucial now?

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.413
General, as we talk about

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.014
what's happening?

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:11.184
But the description there is

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.886
that it is an urban style of warfare

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.121
that they are.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.089
The Ukrainians,

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.490
they say
that they are committed to it,

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.725
but President Zelensky says

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.159
not at any cost.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.527
I mean, what do they need?

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:26.132
And is part mood more of a strategic win?

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.334
Or is it something of a momentum

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.669
win, a symbolic win

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:30.970
for Russia and for the

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.507
victor?

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:38.011
But mood is important.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:40.480
I would say that it is

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.949
at the tactical operational level,

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.184
important to the Ukrainian defense.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:48.688
But I think for Russia and Ukraine,

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.089
this is a fight

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.758
that has really evolved

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:54.060
and do something is symbolic.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.762
And if you remember,

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:56.663
sort of against

00:04:56.663 --> 00:05:00.166
odds, Ukrainians held on to back, moved

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:01.934
through the period

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:05.672
of the 24 February one year anniversary.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.941
Putin basically got no trophy win, no win

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:12.345
to show Moscow for that.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:16.416
I think tactically, yes, it's

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.684
a lot of significance.

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.651
However,

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.353
if the Ukrainians decide

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.555
to make a tactical withdrawal,

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.656
it's not a strategic

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.358
withdrawal of the Russians

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.125
pulling back from

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:26.726
their son

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.428
was a strategic result withdrawal.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.529
If they do,

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:32.365
they will fall back on successive

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.333
defense lines.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.501
Yes, it'll make more

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.071
links between towns in that area,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.273
more challenging

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.641
But it is certainly not

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:44.077
the end of the war in the Donbas.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.311
So they can

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.914
but they have exacted a terrible toll

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:48.881
on the Russians.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.017
But the Russians also

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.553
and in the Donbass area,

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.355
have the Russians in a bit,

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.990
excuse the metaphor of a bear hug.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.192
So what becomes

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.560
the most important near-term

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.661
the nuts and bolts?

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:02.762
Artillery.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:06.032
Artillery rounds, one 55 millimeter

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:10.436
em, 77 artillery rounds up, more stingers

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:11.938
which will knock down

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:12.605
low flying

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:13.806
Russian jets

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.308
that intimidate their pilots

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:17.110
to come in and support.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.411
So it's a tough fight.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.747
Ukrainians have given an amazing amount.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.782
If they ultimately withdraw,

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:24.650
they have exacted their toll.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.085
They held it through this

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.687
critical period. And

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.623
yes, it's hard to give up.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:31.524
But they give they

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:34.026
they finally gave up Mariupol.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.729
And and I think this will be talked

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:39.265
as a as a as a victory.

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:41.501
Well,
Ukraine also has to be mindful

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:42.902
of not exhausting its manpower

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.604
and its artillery as it's preparing

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:45.938
for its counter-offensive,

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.874
which suggests to happen

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.509
sometime in the spring.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.777
Kim another issue

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:51.744
that's going to come up in

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.146
that is probably coming up

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:55.381
in the hours ahead in the conversation

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.183
between the president and Schultz.

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.317
And we've been talking about it

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.453
at great length here is China.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.589
And the United States is showing

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.124
that they have intel,

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:06.993
that the China is seriously thinking

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:07.693
about providing

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:08.394
lethal aid

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:12.298
to Russia in terms of preventing that.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.567
It's not just the United States

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.502
that can hold any leverage over China.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:17.537
It's Europe as well.

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:20.840
And arguably Germany, its largest

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.141
trade partner.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.344
Absolutely.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.712
Germany needs China

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:28.948
for trade and vice versa.

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.616
And what the Biden administration

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:31.617
has always talked about

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.085
is one of their key ways

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.253
of trying to influence

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.388
China

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:37.990
will be to bring the allies together

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.425
in terms of market

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.194
strength and say, China,

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:42.261
if you want our business,

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.630
you've got to follow international norms.

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:47.066
So this could certainly be a way

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:48.901
of drilling down onto a specific

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:49.502
You know, China,

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:51.003
if you want our continuing business,

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.538
you are not going to arm

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:54.407
Russia in this continuing

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:56.175
evasion invasion.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:59.178
It is also a chance to go

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:01.681
for the two men to talk about

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.015
those F-16s.

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.418
Just as an aside, that keeps coming up.

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:06.986
You know, Biden did get a chance

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:09.255
to have a one on one with Zelensky

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:11.624
where assurances would have been made,

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:13.326
promises likely would have been made that

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:15.161
no, if you give us these jets,

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:16.496
we won't use them to attack

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.498
Russia and escalate the war

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:19.298
that perhaps

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.533
is something that Biden would feel

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.301
most comfortable explaining to

